cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The parity conjecture for independence polynomials of generalized Petersen graphs is false"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattacharjee
    given-names: Deep
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0466-750X"
    affiliation: "Formerly, Electro-Gravitational Space Propulsion Laboratory (EGSPL), Bhubaneswar, Odisha 751030, India"
    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/eConjectureGPParity"
keywords:
  - independence polynomial
  - real roots
  - generalized Petersen graph
  - graph isomorphism
  - counterexample
abstract: >-
  It has been conjectured that for n >= 2k+1 the independence polynomial of
  the generalized Petersen graph GP(n,k) has only real roots if and only if k
  is even. We show that the statement contradicts itself: GP(n,2) is
  isomorphic to GP(n,(n-1)/2) whenever n = 3 (mod 4), and (n-1)/2 is then
  odd. We also show that each direction fails on its own, at GP(7,3) and at
  GP(9,2).
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Parity-dependent real-rootedness in independence polynomials of generalized Petersen graphs"
    authors:
      - family-names: Pandey
        given-names: R.
    year: 2026
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.03293"
